      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "This dashboard demonstrates the Explore logs volume histogram for issue #782: `default.test_logs_volume` holds 270,000 log rows spread across the last 7 days, and the histogram Explore draws above the log lines is now a full-range, server-side aggregate that the plugin computes with a single ClickHouse query instead of approximating client-side from the visible page of logs.\n\n1. Open the **Application logs** panel menu below and choose **Explore**, or click the dashboard link **Open in Explore** above.\n2. The histogram above the log lines is stacked by level, and the old warning *\"This datasource does not support full-range histograms\"* no longer appears.\n3. The **Logs volume by level (server-side aggregate, same SQL Explore runs)** panel below reproduces the exact SQL the plugin sends to build that histogram."
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.3.1",
      "title": "About this demo",
      "type": "text"
